> f(a: u8, b: u8, c: u8) = (a + b) * c
> g(a: u8, b: u8, c: u8) = c * (b + a)
> equiv f g
f and g are equal on the domain of f (proved by algebra: both sides expand to one polynomial in a, b, c mod 2^8)
> equiv g f
g and f are equal on the domain of g (proved by algebra: both sides expand to one polynomial in c, b, a mod 2^8)
